    <div class="component notes col-12">
        <div class="component-content">
<h5 class="field-title">References</h5><ul>
    <li>Barsky, Robert, Alejandro Justiniano, and Leonardo Melosi,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/aea/aecrev/v104y2014i5p37-43.html">&ldquo;The Natural Rate and its Usefulness for Monetary Policy Making,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;<em>American Economic Review: Papers and Proceedings</em>&nbsp;104, May 2014, pp. 37-43.</li>
    <li>Clark, Todd E., and Sharon Kozicki< rel="noopener noreferrer" a="" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/p/fip/fedkrw/rwp04-08.html" />, &ldquo;Estimating Equilibrium Real Interest Rates in Real Time,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>North American Journal of Economics and Finance</em>&nbsp;16, 2005, pp. 395-413.</li>
    <li>Giannoni, Marc P.,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/cup/macdyn/v6y2002i01p111-144_02.html">&ldquo;Does Model Uncertainty Justify Caution? Robust Optimal Monetary Policy in a Forward-Looking Model,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;<em>Macroeconomic Dynamics</em>&nbsp;6, 2002, pp. 111-141.</li>
    <li>Giannoni, Marc P.,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/p/nbr/nberwo/11942.html">&ldquo;Robust Optimal Monetary Policy in a Forward-Looking Model with Parameter and Shock Uncertainty,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;<em>Journal of Applied Econometrics</em>&nbsp;22, 2007, pp. 179-213.</li>
    <li>Laubach, Thomas, and John C. Williams,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/tpr/restat/v85y2003i4p1063-1070.html">&ldquo;Measuring the Natural Rate of Interest.&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;<em>Review of Economics and Statistics</em>&nbsp;85, 2003, pp. 1063-1070.</li>
    <li>Orphanides, Athanasios, and John C. Williams,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/moneco/v54y2007i5p1406-1435.html">&ldquo;Robust Monetary Policy with Imperfect Knowledge,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;<em>Journal of Monetary Economics&nbsp;</em>54, 2007, pp. 1406-1435.</li>
    <li>Orphanides, Athanasios, and John C. Williams, &ldquo;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/bin/bpeajo/v33y2002i2002-2p63-146.html">Robust Monetary Policy Rules with Unknown Natural Rates</a>,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Brookings Papers on Economic Activity</em>&nbsp;2, 2002, pp. 63-145.</li>
    <li>Reifschneider, David, and John C. Williams,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/fip/fedbcp/y2000p936-978.html">&ldquo;Three Lessons for Monetary Policy in a Low-Inflation Era,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;<em>Journal of Money, Credit, and Banking</em>&nbsp;32, November 2000, Part 2, pp. 936-966.</li>
    <li>Taylor, John B.,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/crcspp/v39y1993ip195-214.html">&ldquo;Discretion versus Policy Rules in Practice,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;<em>Carnegie-Rochester Conference Series on Public Policy</em>&nbsp;39, 1993, pp. 195-214.</li>
    <li>Taylor, John B.,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/p/nbr/nberwo/6768.html">&ldquo;A Historical Analysis of Monetary Policy Rules,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;in J.B. Taylor, ed.,&nbsp;<em>Monetary Policy Rules</em>, Chicago: University of Chicago Press, 1999, pp. 319-341.</li>
    <li>Wicksell, Knut,&nbsp;<em>Interest and Prices</em>, 1898.</li>
    <li>Woodford, Michael,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/fip/fedkpr/y2012p185-288.html">&ldquo;Methods of Policy Accommodation at the Interest-Rate Lower Bound,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City 2012 Economic Policy Symposium,&nbsp;<em>The Changing Policy Landscape</em>.</li>
    <li>Wu, Tao,&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" class="offsite" target="_blank" href="https://ideas.repec.org/a/fip/fedfel/y2005ioct21n2005-27.html">&ldquo;Estimating the &lsquo;Neutral&rsquo; Real Interest Rate in Real Time,&rdquo;</a>&nbsp;Federal Reserve Bank of San Francisco,&nbsp;<em>Economic Letter</em>, No. 2005-27, October 21, 2005.</li>
</ul>        </div>
    </div>
